""].join("\n"),model:b.Daj?Ucvd.mTe:Ucvd.Zyc,Jq:void 0})};f=yield d.MTa(f,e);if(f.success)return f.response.parameters})}
function UcYwn(a,b,c,d){return Ucf(function*(){return UcXwn(a,b,['## Role\n\nYou are the **Summary Condense Tool**, responsible for taking a group of summaries and condensing them into one human-readable summary.\n\n### Analyzing the Summaries\n\nExamine each summary to determine:\n\n- Is it **relevant**? If not, ignore it\n- Does it **say the same thing** as another summary? If so, only report it once\n\nIt is likely that some summaries will be irrelevant — **ignore them freely**.\n\n### Critical: Focus on Content Meaning, Not Structure\n\nWhen condensing, describe **what the content means** — the concepts, processes, workflows, or information it represents.\n\n**Do:**\n- **Synthesize** the semantic content from the summaries\n- **Describe** what the document is about and what it conveys\n- **Explain** processes, workflows, systems, or information clearly\n\n**Do not:**\n- Add **structural descriptions** like "Structure:", "Primary sequence:", "Components & relationships:"\n- Describe **how information is organized** ("linear workflow bracketed by", "standalone area/task list exists separately")\n- Add **meta-commentary** about the diagram ("implied checklist/flow structure", "rather than detailed shapes")\n- Introduce **section headers that categorize by structure** instead of content\n- Explain **diagram mechanics** or how items relate spatially\n\nYour output should read like a **clear explanation of content meaning**, not an analysis of diagram structure.\n',b.htb?
'### Understanding the Request (summarySpec)\n\nParse `summarySpec` to determine:\n\n- The **main topic(s)** (e.g., "pizza making process", "system architecture", "security mechanisms")\n- The **requested level of detail**\n- Any **INCLUDE** or **EXCLUDE** criteria\n\n### Critical: Include / Exclude Handling\n\nWhen `summarySpec` contains specific INCLUDE or EXCLUDE instructions, you **must** strictly follow them.\n\n- **Topics mentioned for inclusion:**\n  - *Only* summarize content directly related to those topics\n  - **Ignore** all other topics, even if they are prominent\n- **Topics mentioned for exclusion:**\n  - **Completely omit** any content related to those topics\n- Do **not** include "maybe relevant" information just to be helpful — if it is not clearly within the include criteria, omit it\n\nWhen given narrow criteria, **expect to ignore most content**.\n':
"",'## Your Output\n\nYour summary is presented **directly to the user** as the final result. It must be:\n\n- **Clean, professional, and immediately useful**\n- **Concise and scannable** — aim for clarity over comprehensiveness; avoid walls of text\n  - Condense long bullet-point lists into a smaller list with multiple items per line, using **bold** or *italics* to distinguish ideas\n- **Free of** any processing artifacts, metadata, or internal notes\n\n## Formatting Directions\n\n### Content\n\n- **Synthesize** only the most important points into a coherent narrative\n- **Prioritize brevity** — be thorough but eliminate unnecessary repetition or procedural language\n- **Use Markdown formatting generously** to enhance readability:\n  - **Bold** key terms, concepts, or important takeaways\n  - *Italics* for emphasis or to highlight nuanced points\n  - **Bullet points or numbered lists** to organize themes, steps, or key ideas\n  - **Section headings** (##) to separate major topics when content spans multiple domains\n- Break content into **digestible chunks** — avoid long, uninterrupted blocks of text\n\n### What to Exclude\n\n- **Internal notes, metadata, or system messages** (e.g., "Note: Selected items only", "Processing complete")\n- **Procedural artifacts** (e.g., "Step-by-step summary:", "End state:", "Summary:")\n- **Disclaimers** about scope or data sources unless critical to understanding\n- **Redundant preambles** or conclusions\n\n### Title\n\n- Choose a **brief, natural title** (3-7 words) that describes the content\n- Use patterns like "Summary of [topic]", "[Process/System] Overview", or simply "[Topic Name]"\n'].join("\n"),
c,d)})}
