Uccxn(this)?"- Use this tool when creating NEW diagrams from scratch, **UNLESS** the request is about a business-specific process, organizational workflow, or SOP that is specific to the user's business (not general public knowledge). If it is such a process, you MUST use the switch_agent tool to route it to the Process Agent. **Do NOT route** well-known public or civic processes (e.g., 'how a bill becomes a law', 'the water cycle') — these are general knowledge, not business-specific workflows, and should be handled directly.":
"- Use this tool when creating NEW diagrams from scratch",'- Use this tool when EDITING or ADDING TO existing diagrams (flowcharts, mindmaps, ERDs, etc.)\n  - **IMPORTANT:** Even if the user says "add ideas", "brainstorm", or similar words, if they\'re referring to an EXISTING DIAGRAM, use THIS tool\n  - For example: "add ideas to my mindmap" or "brainstorm more nodes for this flowchart" means EDIT THE DIAGRAM, so use this tool\n- The user will often ask to edit an existing diagram in some way. There are tools that can do simple text replacement, but when the user is asking for part of an existing diagram to have more detail or be removed or be reconnected in some way use this tool.\n- It is better to call this tool for editing a diagram than to call the EditText or AddBlock tools when there is ambiguity.',
()=>Uccxn(this)?"- If the user asks to map out, diagram, or document a business process, operational workflow, or SOP that is specific to their business (not general public knowledge) — whether they type the details in chat, attach a document, or ask to start from scratch — DO NOT use this tool. You must invoke switch_agent to hand the request to the Process Agent. **Exception:** Well-known public or civic processes (e.g., 'how a bill becomes a law', 'the water cycle') are general knowledge, not business-specific, and should be handled directly with this tool.":
"- This tool will be able to see the **entire conversation history**. In particular it will be able to see files the user has attached. If the user is asking to generate a diagram from an attached document, this is probably the right tool to call.","## Clarifying Questions\n\n- If the tool does not have enough information, it responds with a **clarifying question** instead of generating a diagram\n- Check the `wasDiagramGenerated` field on the result:\n  - `true` — a diagram was generated\n  - `false` — no diagram was generated; a clarifying question was asked instead\n- If a clarifying question was asked, **inform the user** that no diagram was generated and display the question\n\n**IMPORTANT:** If the tool call to generate the diagram is already part of the chat history, do **not** create a new call for it — a duplicate call is redundant and unnecessary."];
